## What upstream did with ours

**Issue 158 only** (the codex-vm UART divisor read as output). Fixed on main
before U65 was cut (29568, 29618, 30741), so it shipped in U65: codex-vm tracks
COM1's LCR and drops 0x3F8 writes while DLAB is set; at U66 no
`codex/test/*.expected` begins with 0x01. Neither Update's notes mention us.

What could move our arms: new refusals CDX4025 (an undecidable proof type,
COMPILER-110) and CDX1080 (constructor return annotations, COMPILER-116);
COMPILER-106/107/108 (closures past six values, integer tables past ~6,000,
record-field calls of seven arguments) from U65; and COMPILER-109, the
128-column layout, with the parser, scoper and resolver rewritten
"token-identical" and the plugs reflowed (most of ZigEmitter's and
WasmEmitter's diff).

